        "affiliation": "Central Research Laboratory, Hitachi, Kokubunji, Tokyo 185, Japan",
        "bio": "Yoshizumi Eto received his B.S.E.E. and Ph.D. degrees both from Tokyo University in 1966 and 1977 respectively.",
        "name": "Yoshizumi Eto"
      },
      {
        "affiliation": "Central Research Laboratory, Hitachi, Kokubunji, Tokyo 185, Japan",
        "bio": "Masuo Umemoto received his B.S.E.E. degree from Kyoto Technical University in 1969. Since joining Central Research Laboratory, Hitachi, Ltd. in 1969, he has been engaged in the research activities for home VTRs, PCM tape recorders, solid state camera and digital VTRs. His research interests are modulation codes and high reliable reproducing circuits for magnetic digital recording. He is a member of the Institute of Television Engineers of Japan. Since joining Central Research Laboratory of Hitachi, Ltd., he has been engaged in developing of home VTRs, TV cameras, facsimile modems and digital TV equipments. Currently, he is a senior researcher of the 5th department in his laboratory, managing the research activities for future digital video recording and TV camera technologies.",
